Recover_Integration_Concrete_Test
├── when caller not owner
│  └── it should revert
└── when caller owner
   ├── when token is native
   │  ├── given pool ETH balance insufficient
   │  │  └── it should revert
   │  └── given pool ETH balance sufficient
   │     ├── it should send the ETH to the owner
   │     ├── it should reduce the pool ETH balance
   │     └── it should emit {Recovered} event
   └── when token is an ERC20
      ├── when token is not a contract
      │  └── it should revert
      ├── when token is the staking token
      │  ├── given recovery leaves pool below total stakes
      │  │  └── it should revert
      │  ├── given recovery leaves pool at total stakes
      │  │  ├── it should send the surplus to the owner
      │  │  └── it should emit {Recovered} event
      │  └── given pool surplus includes unclaimed rewards
      │     └── it should let the owner recover the rewards
      └── when token is another ERC20
         ├── it should send the tokens to the owner
         ├── it should leave the staking accounting untouched
         └── it should emit {Recovered} event
